{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/405159-what-additional-gift-would-you-add-to-the-corebook","id":405159,"title":"What additional Gift would *you* add to the corebook?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-13T15:10:01-08:00","id":405159,"title":"What additional Gift would *you* add to the corebook?","content":"So, forumgoers, a question for you!<br /> <br /> The 2e corebook obviously has the 5 Moon Gifts, the Wolf Gifts, and then the 15 Shadow Gifts - the same 15 'other' Gifts as in 1e. I would dearly have loved to add more but there was no way in hell I would have managed that without seriously cutting down the other Gifts to compensate, sadly.<br /> <br /> However, theoreticals are not restricted by such trifles, so I ask you, forum, what *one* (or two if you really can't choose) Gifts would you add to the core 15 if you had godlike power over the laws of word count? Don't worry too much about what has to make up their Facets and mechanics specifically, and <i>don't</i> worry about sticking to Gifts from 1e or about sticking to what those Gifts did.<br /> <br /> What always struck you as a missing piece of the Gifts puzzle? When you had trouble finding a Gift that matched the concept of a given spirit and what it ought to be able to grant to Uratha, what Gift would have patched that hole? Or what Gift idea is just too plain cool not to go in?<br /> <br /> For me? Well, it'd have to be a City Gift; if I'd just had the word count for one more Gift, it'd have been City that I'd have gone with. For one, it nicely helps counterbalance Nature and Weather as different aspects of the world around the Uratha that they can draw upon, offers an excellent Gift for various urban spirits to know, and the 1e City Gift is pretty damn cool and would serve as an excellent base for a 2e-style Facet set.<br /> <br /> Running a close second would be Sea - after all, much of the world's surface is ocean, and I think there's a fair bit more mileage to work with than just the Water Facet of the Gift of the Elementals!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T16:57:58-08:00","id":405290,"title":"","content":"I'd have to agree on City. Most of the games I play are very centered on large cities, and having that there to be manipulated helped bring out the sense wildness to the place that the presence of Nature and Weather evoked for the more rural settings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T18:23:42-08:00","id":405371,"title":"","content":"Yeah, City was the first that came to my mind, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T18:39:06-08:00","id":405376,"title":"","content":"I also agree with city. It is an awesome list, and my players used some of those gifts constantly. City Eyes especially. If that one isn't in the core book, I'll make it up by myself.<br /> <br /> I have also been thinking of making a &quot;Gift of Iron&quot; or &quot;Gift of Stone&quot;.A concept that implies strength, anyhow.<br /> My highly sketchy ideas this far would be something like this:<br /> Purity: Repair something that was broken.<br /> Glory: Give yourself armor<br /> Honor: Not sure how to make the rules for this, but I thought something along the lines of making the character immovable by external forces. No tripping or knockdown or anything. <br /> Wisdom: Increase equipment or weapon modifier for simple tools and weapons.<br /> Cunning: Reduce the durability or armor of an object.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T18:52:53-08:00","id":405382,"title":"","content":"A Sea gift would be cool, there's very little to do with the oceans across all of the gamelines. The City gifts we had were pretty cool, it would be nice to see them updated but to be honest since my first game isn't taking place in a city I'd have to be mercenary and choose something else.<br /> <br /> I'd prefer something that could be used for outsider and antagonist wolves, if only as building blocks or a view at the world beyond the Forsaken and Pure. So while I'd like to see a new version of Tainted Moon (I said Eclipse originally but Lyrics' post reminded me) gifts, with powers working antithetical to the five auspices, that's more of a direct opposition to the Forsaken. In the end I guess I'd like to see Sun gifts. We don't know much about Helios except that it takes a larger role in the new game, and it stands to reason that while he may not like the Forsaken or the Pure there are probably some wolves that have fallen under the sway of the sun. While the gifts could normally be open to things like the Apollo-worshipers in Acrozatarim's Parisian chronicle, they could also be gained by player werewolves after significant acts.<br /> <br /> I asked my wife and she offered Digital gifts, the internet and digital spirits probably becoming a more common thing in modern times. She also suggested Family gifts, which led to a hypothetical scenario where one werewolf announces to the pack something to the extent of, 'Gray Walks-In-Rain, you are not the father,' causing him to burst out dancing while Jenna Skycrawler runs away waving her arms and wildly objecting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-13-2015, 10:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T19:04:11-08:00","id":405384,"title":"","content":"I agree that city gifts would be good, however I feel were missing tainted moon gifts for the bale hounds. The pure can be supplimented by anything, but bale hounds are on their own. I suppose it wouldn't be hard to convert what was in blasphemies to the new style, it's already split into 5 phases...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T19:28:08-08:00","id":405398,"title":"","content":"I second (third? Fourth?) City. <br /> <br /> One thing that I always thought was lacking, though, was a Gift of &quot;Toughness&quot;, or &quot;Endurance&quot; or similar. Something for faster healing and/or more Stamina, and maybe with facets for inspiring packmates or lending your physical ability to others, or for extra resistance to Numina. Something to actually make the Storm Lords that unstoppable endurance-monkeys that they paint themselves to be, *without* having to dump all their attributes into Stamina.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T19:33:43-08:00","id":405400,"title":"","content":"There's an <a href=\"http://wodindex.wikispaces.com/Complete+Werewolf+the+Forsaken\" target=\"_blank\">Endurance gift tree</a> in The Rage. But it would be nice to see it or something like it updated to 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-13-2015, 10:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T22:59:30-08:00","id":405478,"title":"","content":"I think a conversion is easier then we're making it. I also just thought of a way to bring in primal form, as a predator king milestone gift (I know they aren't in 2e but lemme dream!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T23:23:17-08:00","id":405490,"title":"","content":"I'm going to have to with the Sea Gift. I love the water, and would love to see more WoD dealing with the Oceans!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If I post any good ideas regarding house rules feel free to use them! Giving me credit is optional! All I want is people to have fun!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4737-afro-luigi","name":"Afro Luigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4737_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T00:06:11-08:00","id":405503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/405159-what-additional-gift-would-you-add-to-the-corebook?p=405400#post405400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's an <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://wodindex.wikispaces.com/Complete+Werewolf+the+Forsaken&amp;quot;]Endurance</a> gift tree[/URL] in The Rage. But it would be nice to see it or something like it updated to 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, whaddaya know? Thanks! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T03:19:36-08:00","id":405631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/405159-what-additional-gift-would-you-add-to-the-corebook?p=405376#post405376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have also been thinking of making a &quot;Gift of Iron&quot; or &quot;Gift of Stone&quot;.A concept that implies strength, anyhow.</div> </div> </div> </div>A few years ago, I ran a Chronicle set in Cornwall for a bit as a break from our main Werewolf game. Part of that was a Lodge of the Stannary, an Iron Master Lodge linked into Cornwall's history of mining, smelting and producing metals that stretches back a good couple of millenia. I knocked together a Gift of the Stannary at the time that was a mixture of underground and metal Gifts in theme. I can't remember what most of them did now, but one of them was Quell Silver that let you reduce incoming silver damage by a certain amount. It's something I'd probably pop into a new Gift of Metal.<br /> <br /> Oh, wow, just found my old notes for the Cornwall game, including all the Rites and Gifts...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T11:57:56-08:00","id":405960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/405159-what-additional-gift-would-you-add-to-the-corebook?p=405631#post405631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, wow, just found my old notes for the Cornwall game, including all the Rites and Gifts...</div> </div> </div> </div>Finding years-old RPG notes is one of the best things about the hobby!<br /> <br /> Any chance you could share some of the ideas you had? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T12:39:26-08:00","id":406030,"title":"","content":"Dark side of the Moon Auspice Gifts (Dreamers, Judge's, Stalkers, Warrior's, Witch's Moons) from Lore of the Forsaken. I used these far more than the core book ones. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Endurance Gifts from Rage were my second thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T14:56:25-08:00","id":406130,"title":"","content":"The Gifts I made the most use of in our last werewolf chronicle, outside the core book Gifts, were the City Gifts. It probably had something to do with the fact that our teritory was a bad neighborhood in a large city.<br /> <br /> Endurance would be my second pick, followed by either the Darkness/Stalking Gifts or the Information Gifts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T08:42:10-08:00","id":409013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NateD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/405159-what-additional-gift-would-you-add-to-the-corebook?p=405398#post405398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I second (third? Fourth?) City.<br /> <br /> One thing that I always thought was lacking, though, was a Gift of &quot;Toughness&quot;, or &quot;Endurance&quot; or similar. Something for faster healing and/or more Stamina, and maybe with facets for inspiring packmates or lending your physical ability to others, or for extra resistance to Numina. Something to actually make the Storm Lords that unstoppable endurance-monkeys that they paint themselves to be, *without* having to dump all their attributes into Stamina.</div> </div> </div> </div>Various of those kinds of things exist as Facets scattered through other Gifts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/405159-what-additional-gift-would-you-add-to-the-corebook?p=405960#post405960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Finding years-old RPG notes is one of the best things about the hobby!<br /> <br /> Any chance you could share some of the ideas you had? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well it has the Sea Gift and Stannary Gift; the Sea Gift would need lots of reworking for a 2e format, while the Stannary Gift was incomplete (I apparently didn't finalise the 4 and 5 dots of it as the player character in the Lodge of the Stannary had other stuff she wanted to spend her XP on).<br /> <br /> There's a load of rites, many incomplete or just a sketched out idea. Interestingly, two of these rites ended up in the 2e corebook in later, evolved forms (one is the sample Blood Talon tribal rite in the book).<br /> <br /> And 7 fetishes, three of which reference a concept that was also further developed later on, and managed to sneak into one of my Hunting Grounds and one of the idigam essence-shaping powers <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/405159-what-additional-gift-would-you-add-to-the-corebook?p=406030#post406030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dark side of the Moon Auspice Gifts (Dreamers, Judge's, Stalkers, Warrior's, Witch's Moons) from Lore of the Forsaken. I used these far more than the core book ones. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Endurance Gifts from Rage were my second thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, we really wanted to fit in two Moon Gifts per Auspice in the corebook but we just didn't have the space in the end; we have future-proofed the rules for doing more Moon Gifts in the future, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/405159-what-additional-gift-would-you-add-to-the-corebook?p=406130#post406130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Gifts I made the most use of in our last werewolf chronicle, outside the core book Gifts, were the City Gifts. It probably had something to do with the fact that our teritory was a bad neighborhood in a large city.<br /> <br /> Endurance would be my second pick, followed by either the Darkness/Stalking Gifts or the Information Gifts.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, Darkness and Stalking seem like funny ones to me, as Darkness is the kinda thing that is already largely covered by the Stealth Gift (and to a lesser extent, the Evasion Gift). Stalking has largely been woven into other Gifts and the Wolf Gifts now, of course. But with spirits of darkness, stealth, quiet and the like already well-served with the Stealth Gift, I'd be more inclined to do a, say, Thirst or Dessication Gift before I did a Darkness Gift - something I can use with spirits of salt, the desert, heat, even sea-water to some extent.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T10:27:41-08:00","id":409085,"title":"","content":"To me, there's a lot, and I do mean a lot, of overlap between Gifts already. I want to see how the Gifts are shaping up first. <br /> <br /> I mean, its more the possible that Endurance is going to be merged with Strength Gifts. And City make its way into the Technology, Knowledge, or Nature gift line. Yes, Nature, because a lot of the Gifts from City really, to me, like a mix of &quot;talking with the urban jungle,&quot; knowledge to know best pathways (repeat of level 4 gift!), and just a curse of technology hating someone. <br /> <br /> So, in light of that, I'm going to wait and see what comes up because it might already be covered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T11:22:54-08:00","id":409144,"title":"","content":"Here's another bale hound gift question: Can they, under the new system, use the same gifts as the other werewolves? Do they also have access to the wolf lists?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T11:31:01-08:00","id":409148,"title":"","content":"Nothing stopped them from doing so in Blasphemies. They still have their Auspices, unless they're also Pure. <br /> <br /> And they're still Uratha, for whom the Wolf Gifts come naturally.<br /> <br /> So I would assume the answer is 'yes'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T11:32:24-08:00","id":409149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/405159-what-additional-gift-would-you-add-to-the-corebook?p=409144#post409144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's another bale hound gift question: Can they, under the new system, use the same gifts as the other werewolves? Do they also have access to the wolf lists?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and yes. All werewolves have access to the Wolf Gifts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T11:34:29-08:00","id":409151,"title":"","content":"I think in blaphemies they could not learn normal gifts... i'll give it a quick look again though, but pretty sure this was a point of contention for me before and i was on the losing end... oh nope you're completely right! &gt;.&gt; Jesus think i'd remember something like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T11:38:39-08:00","id":409173,"title":"","content":"Anything you can do, they can do also. And then some.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T13:34:12-08:00","id":409272,"title":"","content":"I think we saw a lot about the Shadow and Lunar gifts already, but are completely oblivious regarding those Wolf gifts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T16:18:38-08:00","id":409394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/405159-what-additional-gift-would-you-add-to-the-corebook?p=409013#post409013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Various of those kinds of things exist as Facets scattered through other Gifts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I've seen them actually (I'm a playtester, and gotta say - I love your work! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> But the only problem is that none of them are Affinity for my character. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T16:36:36-08:00","id":410729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/405159-what-additional-gift-would-you-add-to-the-corebook?p=409272#post409272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we saw a lot about the Shadow and Lunar gifts already, but are completely oblivious regarding those Wolf gifts.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are three Wolf Gifts, so there's 15 Wolf Facets available. That's all I'll say for now <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NateD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/405159-what-additional-gift-would-you-add-to-the-corebook?p=409394#post409394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I've seen them actually (I'm a playtester, and gotta say - I love your work! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> But the only problem is that none of them are Affinity for my character. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well if you're playing a Storm Lord then there's a suitable Facet in Weather, plus one in ... the Hunting Wolf Gift? It may have moved from there when we added in the third Wolf Gift and reshuffled the Facets a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T18:26:33-08:00","id":410875,"title":"","content":"I see Ghost Wolves investing a lot in the Wolf Gifts just because of how easily they come by comparison.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T12:48:12-08:00","id":411928,"title":"","content":"While I'm not sure how this would work exactly, the idea of a Gift that benefits hunting supernatural targets in a general sense(one Facet might, I don't know, add the appropriate Renown to your Resistance attributes for the sole purpose of contesting or subtracting from a power's activation role?) might be nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T12:53:43-08:00","id":411936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/405159-what-additional-gift-would-you-add-to-the-corebook?p=411928#post411928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I'm not sure how this would work exactly, the idea of a Gift that benefits hunting supernatural targets in a general sense(one Facet might, I don't know, add the appropriate Renown to your Resistance attributes for the sole purpose of contesting or subtracting from a power's activation role?) might be nice.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, in first edition we had scent of taint, which was great at hunting other supers. Not perhaps at fighting them, but you sure got better at hunting them. <br /> <br /> But a power designed to enhance resistance pools could be something, yes. Mage had it, in the case of Mind Shield, so there are precedents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T13:50:37-08:00","id":412036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/405159-what-additional-gift-would-you-add-to-the-corebook?p=410729#post410729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are three Wolf Gifts, so there's 15 Wolf Facets available. That's all I'll say for now <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Three Wolf Gifts?! AWESOME. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T05:30:36-08:00","id":415049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/405159-what-additional-gift-would-you-add-to-the-corebook?p=411936#post411936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well, in first edition we had scent of taint, which was great at hunting other supers. Not perhaps at fighting them, but you sure got better at hunting them.<br /> <br /> But a power designed to enhance resistance pools could be something, yes. Mage had it, in the case of Mind Shield, so there are precedents.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a new, better version of Scent of Taint; and there is a Facet that does some of what you want on the latter point as well, in inspiration irc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/405159-what-additional-gift-would-you-add-to-the-corebook?p=412036#post412036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Three Wolf Gifts?! AWESOME. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yup.<br /> <br /> We started out with two (Hunting &amp; Change) but a third got added when we realised we had one more Facet we needed to slot into the Wolf Gifts and no space in the existing two. So an entire extra Gift was added along with five new Facets and a general reshuffle across the three Gifts to make sure things were all in the right place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.co